= Intra-Party Relations

The Cooperative Commonwealth Federation is a collective, formed by various provincial wings and an overlaying National wing. Each is distinct in it's own way so our relationship with each provides leverage at the national level of the CCF and information we could use in our own fight. We may spend resources in this endeavour. 

To whom should we send aid?

- @manitoba_ccf_relations: The pragmatic Manitoba wing will give us insight into the matters of electoral negotiating
- @alberta_ccf_relations: The Alberta wing requires our help the most
- @bc_ccf_relations: Let's help the British Columbia wing; their Marxist tendencies could serve as an inspiration to us
- @national_ccf_relations: True change can occur only at the Federal level - send aid to Ottawa
- @skip_intraparty_relations: Let's not send aid right now
- @easy_discard

@manitoba_ccf_relations
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: ccf_m_relation += 5; ccf_m_strength += 5; resources -= 1; reformist_strength += 5; reformist_dissent -= 10; true_socialist_dissent += 5

The Manitoba CCF is a more moderate wing of the CCF and in somewhat of a fusion/struggle with the provincial ILP. It remains to be seen which of the two will become the dominant force of the democratic left in Manitoba. 

The moderates within our party are satisfied by our attempts to court the pragmatic Manitoban party. 

The Manitoba wing is thankful for our aid.

@bc_ccf_relations
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: ccf_bc_relation += 5; ccf_bc_strength += 5; resources -= 1; true_socialist_strength += 8; true_socialist_dissent -= 10; reformist_dissent += 10

The British Columbia CCF is a more radical wing of the CCF, influenced by it's roots in the Socialist tradition that predated the CCF through the Socialist Party of British Columbia and various provincial Labour parties. 

The True Socialist faction is invigorated by our attempts to court these coastside radicals.

The British Columbia wing is thankful for our aid.

@alberta_ccf_relations
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: {! 
Q.ccf_a_relation += 5; 
Q.ccf_a_strength += 5; 
Q.resources -= 1; 
!}

[? if year >= 1935 : The Alberta wing is struggling to remove the Social Credit Party from power. Even with our aid, it is unlikely that they will ever amount to more than a half dozen MLAs. ?]

[? if year < 1935 : The Alberta wing is one of our prairie sisters, it too borne from primarily rural discontent with the establishment parties. It is currently composed of the governing UFA and the DLP. ?]

The Alberta wing is thankful for our aid.

@national_ccf_relations
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
on-arrival: ccf_nat_relation += 5; ccf_nat_strength += 5; resources -= 1;

The National CCF is the key to the future. While our provincial wings may well do good for themselves at the subnational level, fundamental change can only occur once we hold Ottawa in the palms of our hands. 

The Federal wing is thankful for our aid.

@skip_intraparty_relations
